# SSSF environment, for a roster stamped with `--harness claude_code`. Copy to
# .env at the target repo root.
#
# THERE IS NO API KEY TO SET for this roster. The Claude Code CLI brings its own
# auth (`claude auth`), and a Claude subscription is enough. An agent you later
# move to `harness: pi` is the one that needs a key here — its `model:` is
# written provider/model-id, and the provider half decides which key, e.g.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY, FIREWORKS_API_KEY or OPENAI_API_KEY.

# Where the sssf skill itself lives. The justfile reads the operational scripts
# (issues, prs, kill, worktrees) and the trace UI from there, and every agent
# keeps its skills somewhere different, so nothing can guess it: install.py
# prints the path it ran from — paste it here. Recipes that only run stamped
# ADWs work without it; `just issues`, `just prs`, `just kill`, `just worktrees`
# and `just obs` do not. Machine-specific, which is why it lives in .env.
SSSF_SKILL=

# Optional overrides
# CLAUDE_PATH=claude               # Claude Code binary if not on PATH
# ENGINEER_NAME=                   # engineer lane label, defaults to git user.name
